1 NOTE {geni:about_me} biography
2 CONT Prince-Bishop Heinrich IV came from the House of Sachsen-Lauenburg. He was the son of Duke Franz I of Saxony-Lauenburg (1543–1581), who converted to Protestantism, and of Sibylle of Saxony. At the age of ten he was already eligibl
2 CONC e for a canon position in Cologne. Heinrich initially studied at the university there, in particular under the law professor Dr. Betzdorf, who was his landlord in Cologne and became his mentor. His training and his later actions w
2 CONC ere mainly influenced by Betzdorf Protestant.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links:==
