1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Boddum Church==
2 CONT Tombstone 2 O. 1650, over parish priest Claus Christensen, born in Skarum paa Mors, died 12 Aug. 1652, 53 years old, and wife Kiersten Pedersdater, born in Hinsels, died 16 □. Öland limestone, 244 × 164 cm, double marginal script 
2 CONC with relief capitals. In the center field, you can see a powerful, lively and skilfully made relief of Christ in clouds on the globe with sword and palm branch, surrounded by four intercessors: Mary, John and two robed men. At the
2 CONC  far end Moses with the Tablets of the Law, and on the other side a bearded man without attributes. There under a two-handled incense vase between trumpet angels, and to the sides two coats of arms, the priest's with a flaming, cr
2 CONC oss-marked heart under a sun and above the inn down helmet: CCS, the wife's with a dove carrying an olive branch, and above the helmet: KPD. The lower part of the middle field is taken up by a large, convex script field in a carti
2 CONC laginous baroque frame with angel heads, containing scriptures in Danish and Latin (Job. 19., Phil. 1. etc.) with relief capitals. Including Hourglass and Cranium. In the corners, ovals with Evangelist figures. In the choir's nort
2 CONC h wall, formerly in the choir floor
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Probate==
2 CONT 69 Kirsten Pedersdatter i Bodum præstegård. 20.10.1696, fol.32. 
2 CONT * Enke efter Anders Andersen [Ringkøbing], præst i Bodum, Ydby og Hurup, [død 1666]. B: 
2 CONT * 3) Anders Andersen Bodum, degn i Nibe og Vokslev 
2 CONT * 4) Maren Andersdatter i Thisted, enke efter Jacob Mouridsen Borchorst, præst [i Brovst og Øster Svenstrup]. 
2 CONT * Første ægteskab med [Claus Christensen Morsing, præst i Bodum, Ydby og Hurup, død 1652]. B: 
2 CONT * 1) Peder Clausen Bodum, præceptor på Tandrup 
2 CONT * 2) Frands Clausen Bodum i Bodum præstegård. 
2 CONT
